
> pi-model-discoverer@0.1.0 test
> tsx --test test/*.test.ts

✔ models.json parsing honors discoverModels opt-in, comments, and trailing commas (1.076083ms)
✔ normalization deduplicates, preserves explicit metadata, modelApis, and conservative defaults (0.202791ms)
✔ discovery sends the resolved credential only to the configured origin with redirects blocked (10.781375ms)
✔ Anthropic catalogs use x-api-key and paginate without following server URLs (0.498ms)
✔ failures never expose response bodies, URLs, or credential-bearing errors (6.578959ms)
✔ malformed saved keys cannot escape through header validation errors (0.38875ms)
✔ cancellation does not issue a request (0.096125ms)
✔ refresh hook restores persisted catalogs offline and persists new ones after fetch (0.357791ms)
✔ Pi's actual extension loader registers the command and discovery hook from models.json (40.862666ms)
✔ loader tolerates a missing models.json (9.6545ms)
✔ native discovery delegates to Pi, selecting only authenticated dynamic providers (0.925792ms)
✔ session-start refresh does not force a network fetch (0.094667ms)
✔ explicit unknown and unauthenticated providers do not cause a refresh (0.080334ms)
✔ refresh reports per-provider failures without leaking native auth errors (0.122291ms)
✔ cancelled refresh is not reported as successful (0.117542ms)
✔ a silently superseded refresh does not claim that new models were published (0.125417ms)
